; DOMAIN: stark-conjecture [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: The Stark Conjecture (base/abelian rank-one and general Stark) is the foundational root of the Stark-unit program. For a finite Galois extension K/k with an Artin character chi and a place, the Artin L-function L_S(s,chi) vanishes at s=0 to an order r determined by the multiplicities of the trivial character in the local decompositions; its leading Taylor coefficient L^*_S(0,chi) equals, up to an algebraic (rational-over-Q(chi)) factor A(chi), a regulator formed from the archimedean absolute values (logarithmic embeddings) of Stark units — distinguished S-units of K. In the abelian rank-one case (Stark's refined conjecture) this predicts the existence of a specific Stark unit epsilon whose Galois conjugates' logarithms produce L'_S(0,chi), with epsilon lying in an abelian extension (giving explicit class field theory / Hilbert's 12th over real fields). Rubin-Stark generalizes to higher rank via exterior powers; Brumer-Stark adds Z[G]-integrality/class-group annihilation; Gross-Stark gives the p-adic exceptional-zero refinement. This is the archetype all three refine.
; Bridge: genesis_rubin_stark (Rubin-Stark is the higher-rank exterior-power generalization of the base Stark leading-term = regulator-of-Stark-units identity) + genesis_brumer_stark (Brumer-Stark adds the integral Stickelberger-annihilation refinement to the base Stark regulator statement) + genesis_gross_stark (Gross-Stark is the p-adic exceptional-zero refinement replacing the archimedean regulator of the base Stark units with a p-adic one).
(= (artin-l-function $chi $S) (euler-product-artin $chi $S))
(= (vanishing-order $chi $S) (mult-trivial-char (local-decomposition $S) $chi))
(= (leading-term $chi $S) (nth-derivative (artin-l-function $chi $S) (vanishing-order $chi $S) 0))
(= (stark-unit $K $S) (distinguished-s-unit $K $S))
(= (stark-regulator $chi $S) (archimedean-regulator (stark-unit $K $S) (log-embedding)))
(= (stark-conjecture) (equal (leading-term $chi $S) (times (algebraic-factor $chi) (stark-regulator $chi $S))))
(= (higher-rank-generalize (stark-conjecture)) (rubin-stark))
(= (integral-refine (stark-conjecture)) (brumer-stark))
(= (p-adic-refine (stark-conjecture)) (gross-stark))